126 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (This is a drone simulator I built in Unity. The main goal was to see if I could create a realistic flight simulation by connecting a real RC radio controller \(a Radiomaster Pocket\) to Unity.)
/Pg 8 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
127 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (The core of the project is a C# script `DroneController.cs`. This script acts as the drone's "flight controller." It takes the processed stick inputs from the radio and turns them into physical forces and torques. I then apply these to a Rigidbody component, allowing Unity's physics engine to simulate all the movement.)
/Pg 8 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
128 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (The simulator accurately models three different flight modes \(Angle, Horizon, and Acro\), incorporates essential input processing features such as expo curves and dead zones \(to provide a realistic feel\), and features a simple On-Screen Display \(OSD\) to display flight data.)
/Pg 8 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
